\section{Governing Constraint}

The central SPEHS‑v1.0 invariant is the curvature‑energy veto:

\[
R(r) > \frac{2G}{c^4} E_{\mathrm{eff}}(r)
\]

where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \( R(r) \) is the local Ricci scalar or contracted curvature invariant,
    \item \( E_{\mathrm{eff}}(r) \) is the effective energy density including
    mass, kinetic, field, and stress‑tensor contributions,
    \item \( G \) is the gravitational constant,
    \item \( c \) is the speed of light.
\end{itemize}

This inequality is enforced at every spatial point and timestep. Violation
triggers a curvature redistribution sweep.

